{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 17, :comments ["<b>And let not his heart turn away.</b> For he will go after his desires." "<b>And silver and gold he shall not multiply for himself.</b> Lest he punish Israel. Now Solomon, who gave silver like stones in Jerusalem — because of his great love for wealth, Israel murmured against him and said, \"Your father made our yoke heavy.\" Some say they murmured because of the buildings, but this is not true, for the Gerim built the Temple, as it is written. And behold, Adoniram, who was over the labor tax, they stoned him at his death."], :book :deuteronomy, :voice :ibn-ezra, :lang :en, :chapter 17, :notes {1 "Resolved הגרים as 'the Gerim' (foreign laborers per 1 Kings 5:32–33); הבית read as 'the Temple.' ויש אומרים rendered as 'Some say.' The syntax of the final sentence about Adoniram is compressed and possibly truncated; translated hyper-literally."}, :source-witnesses [["On Your Way" "http://mobile.tora.ws/"]], :timestamp "2026-07-09T18:23:53.203977218Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}